### 2026-09-18 · 004 · Ingest and the coordinate proof (M3)
AGENT     claude-opus-5 (session c78670a9)
STATE     done
TOUCHED   api/ingest.py, api/main.py (/debug/ingest, text-layer gate),
          corpus/letters/scanned_no_text.pdf
VERIFY    fixture boxes vs live extraction → max deviation 5e-6 (JSON rounding)
          pdf.js viewport vs PyMuPDF page.rect → agree at 0/90/180/270
          rasterized PDF → 422, not vision-derived numbers
SUMMARY   Per-character boxes via PyMuPDF rawdict, so substring narrowing is
          exact rather than interpolated from font metrics. Fixture geometry is
          now generated by running real ingest over the real PDF.
ACTIVE    none
NEXT      pdf.js rendering + the visual validator
NOTES     THE trap in this stack: PyMuPDF reports geometry for the UNROTATED
          page, pdf.js applies /Rotate when building a viewport. Left alone,
          every highlight on a rotated PDF lands wrong. Fixed with
          page.rotation_matrix, normalizing against rotated dimensions.
          Verified at 180° the box flips to exactly 1−original on both axes.
          Also: `import fitz` is deprecated — use `import pymupdf`.


