          try to bundle it through Next.


### 2026-09-18 · 006 · Secret and student-data guard
AGENT     claude-opus-5 (session c78670a9)
STATE     done
TOUCHED   .gitignore, scripts/check_secrets.sh, .githooks/pre-commit,
          .env.example, README.md
VERIFY    scripts/check_secrets.sh --all → clean; four attack cases blocked;
          real `git commit` with a planted AWS key → aborted
SUMMARY   Three layers: hardened .gitignore, a pre-commit scanner over staged
          content (so `git add -f` is still caught), and self-healing hook
          installation via npm install. Blocks key-shaped strings, .env files,
          oversized files, and PDFs outside fixtures/ | corpus/letters/.
ACTIVE    none
NEXT      live extraction
NOTES     The PDF rule is a PII guard, not tidiness: aid letters contain student
          data (master context 6.11). Real letters go in uploads/ (gitignored)
          and stay there. Bare `.env.local` in a gitignore does NOT cover
          `.env.production` — the pattern needs `.env` plus `.env.*`.


### 2026-09-18 · 007 · Live extraction and the admission gate (M4)
AGENT     claude-opus-5 (session c78670a9)
STATE     handoff — code complete, live API call never executed
TOUCHED   api/extract.py, api/evidence.py, api/normalize.py, api/main.py,
          api/models.py, api/tests/test_evidence.py, api/tests/test_normalize.py
VERIFY    .venv/bin/pytest api/tests -q → 25 passed
          /analyze without a key → honest 503 (NOT a fixture)
SUMMARY   Claude adapter behind a Protocol; numbered text lines are the
          authoritative source and page images are labelled layout context in
          the prompt. Model output is schema-validated by messages.parse, then
          every claim runs the admission gate before it can become a fact.
ACTIVE    none
NEXT      Add ANTHROPIC_API_KEY to api/.env and run one real extraction against
          fixtures/sample_offer.pdf. Compare the result to the committed
          fixture — they describe the same document, so they should broadly
          agree. Then M5 (multi-layout corpus).
NOTES     Three corrections from reading the SDK reference rather than working
          from memory: use client.messages.parse(output_format=PydanticModel),
          NOT forced tool use; model is claude-opus-5 (do not downgrade — this
          call IS the product); the cost/aid discriminated union had to be
          flattened to one shape with a `kind` field, because strict JSON
          schema handles a single object far better than anyOf.
          normalize.py also carries a DETERMINISTIC rollup guard: an item equal
          to the sum of its siblings is treated as a total even if the model
          forgot to flag it. There is a test that strips every is_stated_total
          flag and confirms the numbers still come out right.


